/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Tresca says yield starts when the largest shear anywhere reaches σY/2.
   - σ1, σ2, σ3 are principal stresses in MPa; σY is the tensile yield strength in MPa.
   - In plane stress one principal stress is zero.
   - von Mises says yield starts when distortion energy — the strain energy that changes shape, not volume — reaches its tension-test value.
   - σ1, σ2, σ3 are principal stresses in MPa; the result is in MPa.
   - For plane stress with σ3 = 0 this becomes σeq,M = √(σ1² − σ1σ2 + σ2²).
   - σx, σy are normal stresses and τxy is shear stress, all in MPa.
   - The 3 on τxy² is not optional.
   - The octahedral plane has a normal making equal angles with the three principal axes.
   - τoct is the octahedral shear stress in MPa; σ1, σ2, σ3 are principal stresses in MPa.
*/
