/* book: lead: Fatigue is failure under a stress that repeats. One application of 500 MPa may be safe; repeated about twenty thousand times, the same stress can start a crack and grow it until the part breaks. The S-N curve records this: stress amplitude S against cycles to failure N. Designers use it for wings, landing gear and engine mounts, where loads reverse in every flight. */
/* book Figure 3.8.1: The steel of worked example 1 on log axes: Basquin’s line S = 900N−0.0587 falls from 600 MPa at 10³ cycles to 400 MPa at 10⁶, then flattens at the 400 MPa endurance limit. At 500 MPa the life is 2.23 × 10⁴ cycles. An aluminium alloy has no flat part; its curve keeps falling (dashed). */
