/* book Worked example 2: Q: The steel of worked example 1 (endurance limit 400 MPa from polished specimens) is made into a machined landing-gear pin. Take a surface factor 0.80, a size factor 0.85 and a reliability factor 0.90. Find the endurance limit of the part and the largest fully reversed stress amplitude it may carry for infinite life with a factor of safety of 1.5.
   1. Corrected endurance limit: Se = 0.80 × 0.85 × 0.90 × 400 = 0.612 × 400 = 244.8 MPa.
   2. Allowable amplitude: Sa = Se/n = 244.8/1.5 = 163.2 MPa.
   3. Compare: the polished test specimen allows 400/1.5 = 266.7 MPa, so the real part loses 39 % of its fatigue strength to finish, size and scatter.
   Answer: Se = 244.8 MPa for the part; allowable fully reversed amplitude 163.2 MPa. */
