/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - One fatigue cycle runs between a maximum stress σmax and a minimum stress σmin, both in MPa, tension positive.
   - σm is the mean stress, the steady part (MPa); σa is the alternating stress, the half-swing about the mean (MPa); the range is σr = σmax − σmin = 2σa.
   - The stress ratio R = σmin/σmax fixes the shape of the cycle.
   - Plot σm across and σa up.
   - Se is the endurance limit (MPa), Su the ultimate tensile strength (MPa), Sy the yield strength (MPa).
   - Goodman is a straight line from Se to Su and the usual conservative choice.
   - The factor of safety n scales both stresses until the load point touches the curve.
*/
